23 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365226 13194139535765 true] [17592186365223 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535765 true] [17592186365223 1041 "field-3" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365223 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365225 13194139535765 true] [17592186365223 1110 #uuid "a087bdc5-b887-593b-bbbe-6bd5d35764d2" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365224 1034 "may not converge to the equilibrium as $t\\to \\infty $" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365224 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535765 true] [17592186365224 1111 #uuid "eaf5eecc-182b-535b-8acd-0e432c31f5fc" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365225 1034 "always converge to the equilibrium as $t\\to \\infty $" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365225 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535765 true] [17592186365225 1111 #uuid "4acf0ee1-86d8-5339-ad3d-9a791b184a97" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365226 1034 "never converge to the equilibrium as $t\\to \\infty $" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365226 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535765 true] [17592186365226 1111 #uuid "6ab58ee0-e242-5617-b1e8-3dadfb4074be" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365227 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365228 13194139535765 true] [17592186365227 1089 "q-335647" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365227 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535765 true] [17592186365227 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t)+2 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={x}^{2}(t)-2y(t)-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of differential equations above?" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365227 1113 #uuid "21ab42b7-8f9f-5826-a8e7-e56da9141cf7" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365227 1145 "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2=0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2y-4=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+2=0\\,⇒\\,y=-x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $y$ into the second equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2y-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2(-x-2)-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+4-4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x & =0 \\\\ x(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\text{ }0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $y:$\n\n- For $x=0,$ we get $y=-0-2=-2.$\n\n- For $x=-2,$ we get $y=-(-2)-2=0.$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium points are\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\,\\text{and}\\,[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365229 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365230 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365231 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365232 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365233 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1041 "selection" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1104 #edb/ref 17592186365231 13194139535765 true] [17592186365228 1110 #uuid "6c00a6fb-3f0f-508f-8224-56362ff2eb1c" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365229 1034 "$[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365229 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535765 true] [17592186365229 1111 #uuid "ee5e9183-0aad-523c-af69-eee680ddb6da" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365230 1034 "$[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ only" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365230 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535765 true] [17592186365230 1111 #uuid "c44ef9cc-e4bd-56e2-9433-6e1702a0ce90" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365231 1034 "$[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365231 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535765 true] [17592186365231 1111 #uuid "fd5ef72d-9708-517b-bf8e-9dcd70a3051d" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365232 1034 "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ only" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365232 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535765 true] [17592186365232 1111 #uuid "d985bc45-5ffa-5643-938e-e6a3042768e2" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365233 1034 "$[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535765 true] [17592186365233 1111 #uuid "39a692a8-9a4d-5345-8ca5-cb9e511c8722" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365234 1017 #edb/ref 17592186365235 13194139535765 true] [17592186365234 1089 "q-335657" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365234 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535765 true] [17592186365234 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+y(t)-1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)={y}^{3}(t)+x(t)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of differential equations above?" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365234 1113 #uuid "5aaeddc8-6572-55ca-bb11-3efda949f182" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365234 1145 "The equilibrium (fixed) points of a system ${x}^{′}(t)=f(x,y)$ are the points for which $f(x,y)=0.$ So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+y-1=0 \\\\ {y}^{3}+x-1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y-1=0\\,⇒\\,x=1-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x$ into the second equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}+x-1 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{3}+(1-y)-1 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{3}-y & =0 \\\\ y({y}^{2}-1) & =0 \\\\ y(y-1)(y+1) & =0 \\\\ y & =-1,\\text{ }0,\\text{ }1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $x:$\n\n- For $y=0,$ we get $x=1-0=1.$\n\n- For $y=1,$ we get $x=1-1=0.$\n\n- For $y=-1,$ we get $x=1-(-1)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium points are\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\text{and}\\,[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535765 true] [17592186365235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365236 13194139535765 true] [17592186365235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186365237 13194139535765 true] [1759218636523